model_runs:
The model is a copy of birds-pass3-model.py at /tmp/claude-1000/-home-alex-code-Bramble-ideation/5369878e-e379-478d-ac97-3201f49297d2/scratchpad/presets/birds-presets-model.py, with outputs run-design.txt, run-B.txt and run-C.txt next to it. With the old 2-turn Swallow it reproduces the saved .out.txt board lines exactly. Changes to the copy:
- every rates.json dial is a parameter;
- amendment 10 (Swallow 1-turn trips) and the built Redwing rule (the largest target count, not a sum) are in;
- B and C field curves: the Sep 2025 mean shape, ramped from R7 to 900 or 1,800 at R12. They feed Jack Daw's steal and the fights;
- a shop-luck jitter ensemble, and a reserves printout.

Results:
- **Design dials, amended:** line A is 551 at R12 (615 before amendment 10) and 586 on the B field.
- **Single dials, B field, paired 200 runs, at R12:**
  - h 2.25 / 2.5 / 3 gives 857 / 1,123 / 1,697;
  - Cuckoo 1/4 gives 716;
  - Redbreast 1/3 gives 682 (54% in one unit);
  - Egg x3 gives 669;
  - Chiffchaff +3 gives 774;
  - Jack Daw 1/2 gives 728;
  - Stork 5 gives 638;
  - recalls, Redwing and golden homecoming give about 0.
- **B:** the jitter median is 966. In fights against the B field, line A wins 75% against the median board at R12 and 22% at R15.
- **C:** the jitter median is 1,969 (C without the Stork step is 1,754). Line A wins 86% at R12 and 57% at R15 against the C field.
- **Cut table and two-Cuckoo probe:** as given in first_cut_dials.
- **Golden-Jay probe with golden homecoming x3:** B reaches 1.24x the field at R12, 1.65x at R14 and 2.17x at R16.

scaling_axes:
Board ≈ bodies + 2 × (sum over non-Shy occupied slots of Rings on that slot × Ring size). All three axes apply, plus time.

- **Count** (Rings on slots), roughly linear in turns and gold:
  - Annis per End of Turn and per sale (fairies_annis_rings, fairies_annis_sale);
  - Nan (fairies_nan_rings);
  - Sally (fairies_sally_rings);
  - Queen's Teind (fairies_queen_rings, fairies_queen_period);
  - pool spells: Spore Cloud 2, Boundary Stone 3.

  B and C raise only Nan.
- **Size** (one Ring size per player, applied back to every Ring already placed). This is where B and C put their power:
  - Cluricaun per tier-up with the rainbow (fairies_ring_growth);
  - Lob when thanked (fairies_lob_growth, fairies_lob_turns);
  - Silky per thank (fairies_silky_growth);
  - Midsummer (fairies_monarch_multiplier, every fairies_monarch_period End of Turns).
- **Applications** (how many bodies take a Ring's stats):
  - Before the fight, each occupied non-Shy slot applies its own Rings once (7 at most). Shy units and gaps apply none.
  - In the fight, the Fetch twin re-applies B1's whole Ring (fairies_fetch_share), Wisps light empty Rings, Reel-Mistress moves a Ring to later attackers (fairies_reel_moves), and the Changeling puts an enemy on your Ring.

  None of these fight-time applications reach the measured board, and they are unchanged in B and C (Fetch at full).
- **Time:**
  - Old Rings grow, so count(t) × size(t) compounds.
  - Midsummer every 3rd End of Turn doubles it, so the curve steps on R14-R16.
  - Lob pays for turns stayed.

The ring line concentrates about 75% of its measured board on B1. The court spreads it, with its biggest unit at about 37-42%.
